#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:89
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Extra Cmake Modules"
msgstr "Instalação dos Módulos Extras do Cmake"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:92
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Extra Cmake Modules</application> by running the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale o &quot;<application>Módulos Extras do Cmake</application>&quot; "
"executando os seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:96
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sed -i '/\"lib64\"/s/64//' kde-modules/KDEInstallDirsCommon.cmake &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"sed -e '/PACKAGE_INIT/i set(SAVE_PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR \"${PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR}\")' \\\n"
"    -e '/^include/a set(PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR \"${SAVE_PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR}\")' \\\n"
"    -i ECMConfig.cmake.in &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sed -i '/\"lib64\"/s/64//' kde-modules/KDEInstallDirsCommon.cmake &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"sed -e '/PACKAGE_INIT/i set(SAVE_PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR \"${PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR}\")' \\\n"
"    -e '/^include/a set(PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR \"${SAVE_PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR}\")' \\\n"
"    -i ECMConfig.cmake.in &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd     build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:109
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a test suite."
msgstr "Esse pacote não vem com uma suíte de teste."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:113
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Unlike other KF6 packages, this module is installed in /usr because it can "
"be used by some non-KF6 packages."
msgstr ""
"Ao contrário de outros pacotes KF6, esse módulo é instalado em /usr, pois "
"ele pode ser usado por alguns pacotes não KF6."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:118
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:121
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>make install</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:126
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:129
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sed ... Modules/KDEInstallDirs.cmake</command>: This command "
"disables applications using cmake from attempting to install files in a "
"<filename class=\"directory\">lib64</filename> sub-directory."
msgstr ""
"<command>sed ... Modules/KDEInstallDirs.cmake</command>: Esse comando "
"desabilita as aplicações que usam o &quot;cmake&quot; de tentarem instalar "
"arquivos em um sub diretório &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">lib64</filename>&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/kde/extra-cmake-modules.xml:136
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sed ... ECMConfig.cmake.in</command>: This command protects the "
"global <application>cmake</application> variable "
"<envar>PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR</envar> from being changed when checking ECM "
"presence: since we install ECM into <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, the check would set that variable to "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, while most KDE packages "
"expect it to be set to <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kf5</filename> and"
" would fail to build if it is set to something else."
msgstr ""
"<command>sed ... ECMConfig.cmake.in</command>: Esse comando protege a "
"variável global do &quot;<application>cmake</application>&quot; "
"&quot;<envar>PACKAGE_PREFIX_DIR</envar>&quot; de ser mudada ao verificar a "
"presença do &quot;ECM&quot;: desde que instalamos o &quot;ECM&quot; em "
"&quot;<filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>&quot;, a verificação "
"configuraria essa variável como &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>&quot;, enquanto a maioria dos pacotes do"
" &quot;KDE&quot; espera que ela esteja configurada como &quot;<filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/kf5</filename>&quot; e falharia na construção se "
"estivesse configurada para outra coisa."

